e":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:59:28-07:00","id":1212002,"title":"","content":"I feel like Turtle should embody continental masses, and thus be massive beyond recognition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:11:59-07:00","id":1212007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1212002#post1212002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Turtle should embody continental masses, and thus be massive beyond recognition.</div> </div> </div> </div>How big are we talking about here? Like island continent big? A la Australia? Or would it be more apt to say a la Lemuria?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:06:39-07:00","id":1212453,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm even more terrified of Turtle now. The writeup is still incomplete, but what's been done so far certainly makes him a Pangaean that few people want to cross.<br /> <br /> =====+=====<br /> <br /> <b><u>TURTLE</u></b><br /> <br /> Though an unfamiliar god to most of the Vinca, this Pangaean is honored by coastal and seafaring tribes in different parts of the world. He is one of the very few denizens of the Border Marches who can pass into the Worlds of Spirit and Flesh without reprisal from Urfarah. Why this is so is a mystery for Uratha and Wise alike, and neither have yet to discover the answer despite generations of attempts.<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> One of the greater gods of the Border Marches, it is said to rival Urfarah in both age and power. Such a claim is backed by the ability to venture out of the Border Marches unchallenged in order to roam not only the Worlds of Spirit and Flesh, but also the realms in-between.<br /> <br /> Many among the Wise and Uratha have tales on why Turtle is given a wide berth by even the Great Predator. Some say that the two Pangaeans clashed in a great battle not unlike the one between Wolf and Bull. Most believe the battle ended at a stalemate, though a few suspect that Turtle was the victor. This belief is fueled by rumors that Turtle found some secret of the Marches which gave him an edge against his fellow gods, including the Wolf herself.<br /> <br /> Whatever the reason may be, Turtle wanders freely as a result, and often travels to a world on either end of Pangaea in pursuit of his own agendas. Not only that, but the Wise have discovered the Pangaean spending much time in the Astral Realm, and even the Ocean Beyond Life.<br /> <br /> Turtle is honored by the People. His animals make their homes in the River, and priests and shamans invoke his name to honor or tame the river-spirits so that their villages thrive. However, he is also called to act as a guide for the dead, so that they may reach the Underworld and make their final descent into its dark waters. Hence, his role is a dualistic one in the pantheon of the gods. Creator and Destroyer. Life and Death.<br /> <br /> Yet despite this reverence, the People are seldom graced by Turtle's presence. The Pangaean secludes himself in the oceans of whichever world he is in. And he seldom strays far from the shore in those few times he sets foot on land. This relative isolation may be another reason why Wolf leaves him be, and it also deters even the most ambitious Wise from attempts to take its heart.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Turtle's vast power is equally matched by his size, to the point that he is often mistaken for an island made wholly of black rock at a distance. The forest that grows from its shell shatters this illusion. Filled with othedworldly coral and vegetation, it provides a home to a multitude of spirits, ghosts, and goetia that Turtle has picked up over the centuries he has travelled.<br /> <br /> Its forays have also made it widely known beyond the Land of the People. The Pangaean will become the basis of the World Turtle archetype found in future cultures around the world. China, India, and North America are but a few examples of the lands where Turtle's memory lives on to an extent.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Turtle is revered by other tribes besides the People. Islanders and seafarers feel the Pangaean's influence more strongly in the waters of their homes, and the Wise among their number often seek him out for knowledge and other boons. These Awakened cultivate spiritual agreements with Turtle and other waterborne gods of the Marches to ensure their survival far from the shores. Such compacts are not always positive, and may demand great sacrifice on the part of the Wise. This, however, is nowhere near the hostility their counterparts in the land-based Vinca incite through their hunts for Omphalos Stones.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Turtle, Calm and Contemplative</u></b><br /> <i>Rank 7 Pangaean</i><br /> <br /> As a Rank 7 entity, Turtle does not operate within the usual rules framework. His capabilities cannot be reduced to a few dice pools, but he possesses several characteristics that are worth noting. Overall, the Pangaean's mere presence can radically influence a scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Influence:</b> Turtles 6, Earth 3, Water 3<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Death 3, Life 3, Fate 1<br /> <br /> If a Storyteller uses the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bChHwxV73epwkgUnDbuAO9Dgjhwcxb93snbibWlCgMY/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\">following House Rules</a> for ephemeral beings, Turtle is treated as a Rank 5 entity with the following traits when struck by his Bane for the first time.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 17, Finesse 16, Resistance 18<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Blast, Drain, Essence Thief, Fate Sense, Implant Mission, Omen Trance, Pathfinder, Resurrection, Seek<br /> <br /> <b>Size:</b> 100<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 218<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 120<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 15<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Turtle must offer audience and refrain from harming anyone who summons him by sacrificing a turtle or turtle spirit through the appropriate rites. He is not bound further if the offer of audience is refused or if the visitor acts against him.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> A spear made from the shell fragments of 225 turtles, with no more than fifteen pieces used for each animal.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Colossus:</b> Turtle is immense of form, a towering god that can simply shrug off lesser attacks. The Pangaean increases his Corpus by his Size, and gains general Armor equal to its Resistance. This armor is completely ignored by attacks made with Turtle's bane. Against creatures and objects of smaller Size than him, his attacks benefit from the 8-Again rule.<br /> <br /> <b>Divine Bleed:</b> The first time in a scene that he suffers Corpus damage, Turtle may reflexively use the Awe, Essence Thief, or Drain Numen for free. Whenever he takes damage, he may use the Mass Create power of Influence (Turtles) for free or create Rank 1 Turtle Spirits based on successes scored in a dice pool equal to the number of points inflicted.<br /> <br /> <b>High Magic:</b> Once per scene, Turtle can spend a Willpower point to cast an improvised spell that is one dot higher than he could otherwise cast.<br /> <br /> <b>Island Beyond Life:</b> In addition to being able to meditate into the Temenos and Anima Mundi, Turtle can do the same to transport into or out of the Ocean Beyond Life. Each instance of this power causes matter from one world to come rushing into the other, including any characters fortunate enough to survive being pulled in.<br /> <br /> <b>Overwhelming Presence:</b> A mortal human who encounters Turtle and realizes they are in his presence suffers an Integrity breaking point. If this roll is failed, the character gains the Madness persistent condition.<br /> <br /> <b>World Turtle:</b> Turtle is aware of the health and emotional state (basic information like fear, pain, hunger, etc) of all turtles and turtle spirits within 225 square miles of his location. Furthermore, he can see through their senses as per the Spirit Dominion Dread Power. If he spends a Willpower point, this power's range is doubled for a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-02-2018, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T10:26:39-07:00","id":1212715,"title":"","content":"Prolly give it something like the Idigam dread power that affords it's size as armor and gives it the 8 again quality in attacks against things of less size. We're talking probably size 100+ like a skyscraper.<br /> <br /> *Pictures packs of Uratha borrowing on Turtle's shell with the Moldywarp facet to end Turtle*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T14:20:03-07:00","id":1212791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1212715#post1212715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prolly give it something like the Idigam dread power that affords it's size as armor and gives it the 8 again quality in attacks against things of less size. We're talking probably size 100+ like a skyscraper.<br /> <br /> *Pictures packs of Uratha borrowing on Turtle's shell with the Moldywarp facet to end Turtle*</div> </div> </div> </div>So, 100 to 120 then in terms of size? I'm going with the chart I linked below as reference.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://wodan.obsidianportal.com/wiki_pages/size\" target=\"_blank\">https://wodan.obsidianportal.com/wiki_pages/size</a><br /> <br /> That's also making me think of all the God of War boss fights that involved tearing through the insides of a monster or god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T15:20:00-07:00","id":1212813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1212791#post1212791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, 100 to 120 then in terms of size? I'm going with the chart I linked below as reference.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://wodan.obsidianportal.com/wiki_pages/size\" target=\"_blank\">https://wodan.obsidianportal.com/wiki_pages/size</a><br /> <br /> That's also making me think of all the God of War boss fights that involved tearing through the insides of a monster or god.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's not a bad idea as far as inspiration goes here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T15:24:46-07:00","id":1212814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1212813#post1212813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's not a bad idea as far as inspiration goes here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Of course, there's the matter of figuring out what would drive werewolves and/or Wise to try to bring down a Pangaean as powerful as Turtle, who happens to be on the level of Wolf, Bull, Bird, and Snake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T16:46:03-07:00","id":1212837,"title":"","content":"Uratha are literally built to do it. Wise stand to gain a lot from the carcass of a Pangaean. Simply an edict from Urfarah on the grounds &quot;you've wandered to your pleasure long enough&quot; would warrant it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:13:01-07:00","id":1213914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1212837#post1212837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uratha are literally built to do it. Wise stand to gain a lot from the carcass of a Pangaean. Simply an edict from Urfarah on the grounds &amp;quot;you've wandered to your pleasure long enough&amp;quot; would warrant it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, hearing that edict and actually acting on it are very different things when you're up against a living island.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, I am wondering what other special abilities I can lump with Turtle. The Colossus Dread Power is definitely a yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T01:32:17-07:00","id":1214476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1049216#post1049216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I wonder, could any of the monsters from the end of Predators be re-fluffed into Pangaeans who turned completely physical?<br /> If so, what were they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading this post again, I kind of wonder what names and titles the Pangaean versions of Tha'hon and Zho'ak would have. I'll probably go with Deep and Breath, but that still leaves me with working out two adjectives to pair alongside them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T11:50:11-07:00","id":1214703,"title":"","content":"How might Lion be classified? And what might be the consideration for him as King of the Beasts?<br /> <br /> Ideas?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T23:16:04-07:00","id":1214933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1214703#post1214703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How might Lion be classified? And what might be the consideration for him as King of the Beasts?<br /> <br /> Ideas?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime (awe-inspiring presence) and/or Life (physical prowess and commanding lesser life forms) for Arcana, I suspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T23:44:50-07:00","id":1214940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1214703#post1214703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How might Lion be classified? And what might be the consideration for him as King of the Beasts?<br /> <br /> Ideas?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'd probably peg him as being either Rank 6 or 7. His arcana spread would probably be like this. -&gt; Prime 4, Life 2 or 3 (depending on Rank). He'd also have an assortment of other powers if we use Acro's unofficial writeups as a reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T07:51:33-07:00","id":1215055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1214940#post1214940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I'd probably peg him as being either Rank 6 or 7. His arcana spread would probably be like this. -&gt; Prime 4, Life 2 or 3 (depending on Rank). He'd also have an assortment of other powers if we use Acro's unofficial writeups as a reference.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you think Wolf could take him? Or, like Turtle, they didn't conflict? In my head I'm imagining King Lion under Emperor Sun as master of the beasts. He'd probably never leave his &quot;place&quot;, and not be someone Wolf would casually pick a fight with. Perhaps even be subordinate to... though that would be a heretical idea to the Urathra.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:35:32-07:00","id":1215073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215055#post1215055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do you think Wolf could take him? Or, like Turtle, they didn't conflict? In my head I'm imagining King Lion under Emperor Sun as master of the beasts. He'd probably never leave his &quot;place&quot;, and not be someone Wolf would casually pick a fight with. Perhaps even be subordinate to... though that would be a heretical idea to the Urathra.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps Lion was to the Sun what Wolf was to the Moon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:47:48-07:00","id":1215079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215073#post1215073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps Lion was to the Sun what Wolf was to the Moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the role of Bull (following the Baal Hadad, at least)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:53:31-07:00","id":1215084,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why Lion would be considered equal or greater. Tiger might be up there (though Father Wolf being theorized as the creator of Pangaea suggests there would be no other contenders). But the idea of lions as 'king of the jungle' came later and wouldn't have any bearing on their Pangaean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2018, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:56:44-07:00","id":1215086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215079#post1215079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's the role of Bull (following the Baal Hadad, at least)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops. <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, a lot of what a lion symbolizes overlaps with what a bull does. Kingship, power, virility, the sun...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:14:28-07:00","id":1215093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215084#post1215084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why Lion would be considered equal or greater.</div> </div> </div> </div>What seems important to me about Lion in regard to Father Wolf is that lions are one of few predators that, like wolves, hunt in pack. It just seem to me that the whole group hunting aspect is important to father wolf. Maybe Lion was born of the mating of Father Wolf(or Mother Wolf) and Saber Thooth Tiger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:26:10-07:00","id":1215169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215093#post1215093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What seems important to me about Lion in regard to Father Wolf is that lions are one of few predators that, like wolves, hunt in pack. It just seem to me that the whole group hunting aspect is important to father wolf. Maybe Lion was born of the mating of Father Wolf(or Mother Wolf) and Saber Thooth Tiger?</div> </div> </div> </div>Urfarah: &quot;<b>What</b> did I drink last night? And how much?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:57:31-07:00","id":1215210,"title":"","content":"Well, Lion came to mind in part because it is one of the oldest represented animals in cave paintings and myth. Even the pairing of bull and lion (depicting the death of bull) is a widespread symbol. Sumerian representations used it, and fixed the zodiac for Bull such that Sun would pass through it during the vernal equinox (spring) and the zodiac for Lion such that Sun would pass through it during the summer solstice. <br /> <br /> This is all to say: you're not wrong, whichever interpretation you want to take for the Sun. It could most accurately be said that Bull represented life and the Lion, war or death. Various sources (and I'm doing a deeper dive as I'm typing) speculate that the motif is perhaps as old as that of the Great Goddess and predates Sumerian civilization by thousands of years. Several (linked I assume) articles assert that &quot;In the symbolic language of Sumer, the lion is the great solar animal.&quot; --That's a pretty strong assertion that I haven't found the JSTOR material to substantiate. <br /> <br /> The point is that Lion is important, and I'm a little surprised he hasn't come up in Pangaean discussion so far.<br /> <br /> And yes, if you go further east, the Chinese replaced Lion with Tiger in the symbolism of rulership animals, just as the terrain of the animals' ranges replaced each other. (Chinese &quot;lions&quot; look more like a kind of dog breed, than they do actual lions.) <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T13:00:41-07:00","id":1215211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215169#post1215169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Urfarah: &quot;<b>What</b> did I drink last night? And how much?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah my first thought is &quot;uhhhh.&quot; And my second is &quot;well if you come from the perspective of 'my myths are preeminent' then werewolves will say whatever makes them feel good.&quot; <br /> <br /> In the modern age, few are going to argue with the wolves about Pangaean myth. It's a moot point that will solve little and likely get you eaten. <br /> <br /> In actuality? Well that would probably depend on the speaker's point of view, no?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T13:23:28-07:00","id":1215219,"title":"","content":"Worship or adoration might have made the lion <i>spirit </i>be important, but it doesn't look like people caring about something makes it any more or less relevant or powerful in regards to it being a Pangaean.<br /> <br /> And Helios is a spirit, I believe they've said Luna and Helios didn't have Pangaean counterparts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is that Lion is important, and I'm a little surprised he hasn't come up in Pangaean discussion so far. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're going for. You can stat it out if you want but most focus is on other entities or areas (Vinca settlements were a few thousand miles north of any lions) because they have pasts tied into the game, like potentially Jaguar, or are tied in with homebrews (a number are progenitors of homebrewed hosts).<br /> <br /> Regarding Pangaean Myth, it's likely modern werewolves have no idea what Pangaea was like, and most of them wouldn't care beyond someone accusing their progenitor from being a lie. But we have pictures of what Pangaea was like from Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> Also Father Wolf apparently mated with just about everything, if the number and origin of Firstborn tells us anything. Tiger or Sabre-Tooth or Jungle Cat doesn't seem that out there. Of course, Pangaea had also been around a long time, and it's entirely possible that something like Lion or other Pangaeans could have been killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2018, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T14:34:26-07:00","id":1215234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215219#post1215219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worship or adoration might have made the lion <i>spirit </i>be important, but it doesn't look like people caring about something makes it any more or less relevant or powerful in regards to it being a Pangaean.<br /> <br /> And Helios is a spirit, I believe they've said Luna and Helios didn't have Pangaean counterparts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... an interesting separation to put a distinction on. I suppose the line of influence flows Pangaean/Spirit -&gt; belief/emphasis -&gt; Spirit. In that Fox was important to the Vinca because Fox was important, and not that Fox was important because Fox was important to the Vinca. <br /> <br /> I use the term interesting for its exact meaning, and not to carry sarcastic or invective undertones. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215219#post1215219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you're going for. You can stat it out if you want but most focus is on other entities or areas (Vinca settlements were a few thousand miles north of any lions) because they have pasts tied into the game, like potentially Jaguar, or are tied in with homebrews (a number are progenitors of homebrewed hosts).</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant just that: that am a little surprised it hasn't come up yet, in published material or homebrew. Again, words used to carry their exact meaning without sarcastic or invective undertones. And I might well try to stat out an entity, hence the original question. The prospect fills me with dread, however....<br /> <br /> Um... need to call you, however, on the geographic distribution matter: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vin%C4%8Da_culture\" target=\"_blank\">Vinca settlement patterns</a> overlap the later Greek and Macedonian settlements who observed lions. More importantly, Panthera leo spelaea was extant throughout Europe and northern Asia, and European lions were observed (rarely) up the 14th century. They went everywhere, and were featured on cave art in France (which is further west, but at the same latitude). <br /> <br /> But you are correct: lion hasn't been <i>important </i>to anything, and as such, hasn't come up for some kind of resolution like Fox, or Bull or even Cat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215219#post1215219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Pangaean Myth, it's likely modern werewolves have no idea what Pangaea was like, and most of them wouldn't care beyond someone accusing their progenitor from being a lie. But we have pictures of what Pangaea was like from Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> Also Father Wolf apparently mated with just about everything, if the number and origin of Firstborn tells us anything. Tiger or Sabre-Tooth or Jungle Cat doesn't seem that out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well ain't that the truth. And yes, I suppose Urfarah getting drunk and having a good time is par for the mythological course. Judging by legends, gods are... promiscuous with their attention.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T15:02:22-07:00","id":1215245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215234#post1215234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use the term interesting for its exact meaning, and not to carry sarcastic or invective undertones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I got it and I appreciate that it's tough to just state things without trying to seem like you're trying to be harsh. But yeah, belief, at least the belief of humans or humanoid things like the Uratha, doesn't seem to have much of or any impact on the Pangaeans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I meant just that: that am a little surprised it hasn't come up yet, in published material or homebrew. Again, words used to carry their exact meaning without sarcastic or invective undertones. And I might well try to stat out an entity, hence the original question. The prospect fills me with dread, however....<br /> <br /> Um... need to call you, however, on the geographic distribution matter: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vin%C4%8Da_culture\" target=\"_blank\">Vinca settlement patterns</a> overlap the later Greek and Macedonian settlements who observed lions. More importantly, Panthera leo spelaea was extant throughout Europe and northern Asia, and European lions were observed (rarely) up the 14th century. They went everywhere, and were featured on cave art in France (which is further west, but at the same latitude).<br /> <br /> But you are correct: lion hasn't been <i>important </i>to anything, and as such, hasn't come up for some kind of resolution like Fox, or Bull or even Cat. </div> </div> </div>I was wrong about the geographic distribution of lions, though our Vinca takes place far north of what would be Sumeria, located near the Balkans.<br /> <br /> Fox's main claim to fame is being a particularly weak Pangaean who got reaped. I'm guessing Bull had a larger part because of his link to the Baal-Hadad of first edition, giving readers something easy to link things to. I'm not entirely sure on this but it's possible Dave Brookshaw based them off of the actual reverence of these animals by the Vinca people.<br /> <br /> For the most part Forsaken isn't about having a whole 'there's a were-thing for every animal' so I'm not sure why you're surprised there isn't mention of a Lion god that existed 7000 years ago, we don't actually have any Pangaeans statted out officially and the only ones in the books are not Pangaeans anymore. If you look at LostLight's first post, most of the Pangaeans mentioned are from homebrews or extrapolated by the existence of hosts. But I do suppose if there is one, it would be mentioned in Changing Breeds (which likely has werelions, being the other side of the 'most part,' or Skinchangers). But it's also possible that Lion did exist and was killed, by Wolf or another Pangaean, or even the Uratha, who are walking, talking banes to all Pangaea-kind and have been existing there for a long time. Looking back at the opening, the developer said it was showcasing the end of their civilization along with the beginning of humanity's. It's possible there were Apocalypse-like werebeast-on-werebeast wars in the Beforetimes.<br /> <br /> As an offhand suggestion you might not sweat it about mechanics and just write the fluff of what you think it would be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2018, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T16:17:18-07:00","id":1215262,"title":"","content":"Speaking of mentions of Tiger, Jaguar, etc, would there be a hypothetical Pangaean of all felines, or one for each recognizable group? Or maybe it\u2019d be like Wolf and the Firstborn, with only one \u201cCat\u201d and her(?) own firstborn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T19:01:22-07:00","id":1215310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215262#post1215262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of mentions of Tiger, Jaguar, etc, would there be a hypothetical Pangaean of all felines, or one for each recognizable group? Or maybe it\u2019d be like Wolf and the Firstborn, with only one \u201cCat\u201d and her(?) own firstborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say one for a generic type of animal. One Turtle, one Cat, one Hyena, so on and so forth. Pangaeans are epic entities that had a Realm all their own. I\u2019d keep their population low, to help preserve their aura of savage grandeur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T19:07:43-07:00","id":1215313,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that &quot;The Sundered World&quot; references Cat as one of the greater gods.<br /> <br /> As a side note, fun thing that I learned today is that the word &quot;deer&quot; once meant &quot;beast&quot;, as in &quot;furry living creature&quot;. Venison meant &quot;that which is hunted&quot;. Nameless animals, like bear (the brown one), or horse (the swift one), are generally taboo or powerful, and animals with antlers or horns are traditionally creatures of power.<br /> <br /> What creature could match Wolf, the Great Predator, God of the Hunt, in power except the Greatest Prey, God of the Hunted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T19:17:18-07:00","id":1215318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215313#post1215313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that &amp;quot;The Sundered World&amp;quot; references Cat as one of the greater gods.<br /> <br /> As a side note, fun thing that I learned today is that the word &amp;quot;deer&amp;quot; once meant &amp;quot;beast&amp;quot;, as in &amp;quot;furry living creature&amp;quot;. Venison meant &amp;quot;that which is hunted&amp;quot;. Nameless animals, like bear (the brown one), or horse (the swift one), are generally taboo or powerful, and animals with antlers or horns are traditionally creatures of power.<br /> <br /> What creature could match Wolf, the Great Predator, God of the Hunt, in power except the Greatest Prey, God of the Hunted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Cat\u2019s already there? I\u2019ll have to reread Dark Eras. <br /> <br /> The Ultimate Prey, matching the Ultimate Predator? Sounds legit. I wonder than what became of Deer, and its children if any. (Or perhaps the role is already covered by Bull?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T01:42:45-07:00","id":1215408,"title":"","content":"I need some thoughts on a possible power that certain Pangaeans may possess.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> * <b>Song of the World:</b> A common power wielded by Pangaeans who frequent the Astral Realm, it allows them to summon the Ecstatic Wind from the World Soul. By spending Essence and a Willpower point to roll Power + Finesse, they can summon the Wind with an intensity based on their Rank. Rank 3 to 4 Pangeans may summon the Wind at Weak Strength, while Rank 5 and 6 do so at Medium Strength. Pangaeans with at least a Rank of 7 can unleash the Wind at its full strength. The power may be invoked in any part of Astral Space, and may last for a number of hours equal to how much Essence is spent to activate this power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T01:57:47-07:00","id":1215412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215318#post1215318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ultimate Prey, matching the Ultimate Predator? Sounds legit. I wonder than what became of Deer, and its children if any. (Or perhaps the role is already covered by Bull?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Deer and Bull would have little in common- Bull is a god of civilization, culture and community. Deer is a god of the wilderness and the hunt. Bull gives parts of himself to support humanity, Deer requires them to show themselves worthy to hunt him and gain his favor. Deer has much more in common with Wolf than with Bull, for at least they speak the same language and have the same understanding of the cycles of the world. Hunt, and be hunted. Chase and be chased. I see Deer has having a strong affinity for Spirit and Life- or perhaps Life and Death. I lean toward the later. The &quot;Horned God of the Hunt&quot; feels appropriate to have both those properties.<br /> <br /> As for possible children- search in google for Wendigo images. I think it would be a good place to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T02:03:41-07:00","id":1215414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215412#post1215412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Deer and Bull would have little in common- Bull is a god of civilization, culture and community. Deer is a god of the wilderness and the hunt. Bull gives parts of himself to support humanity, Deer requires them to show themselves worthy to hunt him and gain his favor. Deer has much more in common with Wolf than with Bull, for at least they speak the same language and have the same understanding of the cycles of the world. Hunt, and be hunted. Chase and be chased. I see Deer has having a strong affinity for Spirit and Life- or perhaps Life and Death. I lean toward the later. The &amp;quot;Horned God of the Hunt&amp;quot; feels appropriate to have both those properties.<br /> <br /> As for possible children- search in google for Wendigo images. I think it would be a good place to start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, yeah you\u2019re right about the Bull being more about civilization. Or at least order. <br /> <br /> But would Wendigo be good children for Deer? I mean, they do have the visual cues, but they\u2019re more Predator than Prey. On the other hand, if we go with Deer indeed having Death, then Wendigos kinda fit them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T02:10:05-07:00","id":1215415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215245#post1215245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not entirely sure on this but it's possible Dave Brookshaw based them off of the actual reverence of these animals by the Vinca people.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBull and Bird/Snake are both so important to the era specifically because of the significance of their depictions in real-world Vinca archaeology.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T02:19:18-07:00","id":1215416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215414#post1215414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But would Wendigo be good children for Deer? I mean, they do have the visual cues, but they\u2019re more Predator than Prey. On the other hand, if we go with Deer indeed having Death, then Wendigos kinda fit them...</div> </div> </div> </div>And no one told you who the father was :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T04:17:00-07:00","id":1215441,"title":"","content":"I just had an idea about a &quot;great prey&quot;-Pangaean. Drawing upon the ideals of both deer, (remember Great Elk was still around by this time), wild boars, as well as things like wild goats and antelopes.<br /> You know, animals that most definitely are prey, but who also are badass beasts that it takes something great to take down. (Elephants, Rhinos, and such are beyond that. They are the land titans.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:44:42-07:00","id":1215489,"title":"","content":"Granted, the Vinca would have had virtually no contact with it, but\u2014-the Leviathan, a whale-Pangaean? The gentle serenity of the sea, barely constraining the ocean\u2019s apocalyptic wrath...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:48:37-07:00","id":1215491,"title":"","content":"Okay, came back after rereading Reflection by Acrozatarim, and I ponder - anybody have more ideas for &quot;conceptual&quot; or &quot;phenomenal&quot; Pangaeans like Harvest and Reflection?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T08:40:13-07:00","id":1215507,"title":"","content":"A solar Pangaean! A \u2018son of the sun\u2019. A great crimson orb, warping gravity (Forces) as it emits killing radioactivity (Prime).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T08:50:41-07:00","id":1215511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215507#post1215507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A solar Pangaean! A \u2018son of the sun\u2019. A great crimson orb, warping gravity (Forces) as it emits killing radioactivity (Prime).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Radioactivity is still Forces. Life, maybe for Sun's life-giving rays? Time, for its role in governing the seasons and calendar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T08:59:12-07:00","id":1215516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215511#post1215511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Radioactivity is still Forces. Life, maybe for Sun's life-giving rays? Time, for its role in governing the seasons and calendar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces and Life, then? The son of the sun is lethal, yet life flowers in his wake!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T09:15:29-07:00","id":1215525,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or every single proposed Pangaean proposed for the last two pages defaults to Prime and Life, because &quot;they're (basically) magical pillars of life yo&quot;.<br /> <br /> If Turtle, for example is so keen on the Astral, why not Mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T09:29:46-07:00","id":1215526,"title":"","content":"Alrighty, then: the son of the sun is the furnace of change (Matter) which brings forth day and night (Time)? A simple solution, just gotta look at different aspects of stars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T09:33:07-07:00","id":1215528,"title":"","content":"&quot;Furnace of change&quot; is Forces. Matter is the Arcanum of stasis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T09:36:19-07:00","id":1215530,"title":"","content":"Famine, a great skeletal undead horror, with a body riddled with devouring insects and a creeping aura of starvation (Death) whose passage brings about karmic doom (Fate) and the loss of all hope (Mind)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T10:08:48-07:00","id":1215540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215528#post1215528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Furnace of change&amp;quot; is Forces. Matter is the Arcanum of stasis.</div> </div> </div> </div>.....color me embarrassed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T15:48:29-07:00","id":1215613,"title":"","content":"The Fourfold King, a great four-headed, eight-armed behemoth that embodies the turning of the seasons (Time) and the wonders of tool-use (Matter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T15:51:25-07:00","id":1215614,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a Pangaean of fungus and rot, personally. Decay, or something like it. Death and time arcana, as entropy and the end of cycles.<br /> <br /> But Pangaeans are pretty much my favorite aspects of Werewolf and Mage blended together, I'd like to see quite a lot. Even been tempted to homebrew a lodge that worships the not quite fully dead remains of a Pangean, some spiritual vestige that clings to the bones acting as the totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T09:24:44-07:00","id":1215825,"title":"","content":"I think that Deer, my hypothetical &quot;Greatest Prey&quot; would have Death as their Arcana. The Influences of Pangaeans are for what they <i>are</i> while the Arcana are what they <i>mean</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Reflection, Bright and Empty</b>, has the Arcana of Prime and, to a lesser extent, Forces. Reflection is perception, and perception is Truth, hence Prime, whereas Forces impacts light. Its Influences are, quite directly, Reflections, but also Water, because water is the primary reflective surface of the Neolithic era.<br /> <br /> <b>Harvest, Watchful and Ravenous</b>, has the Arcanum of Matter. Matter is about the manipulation and categorization of resources, which is very much Harvest's jam. Their Influences are Hunger and Foraging, because Harvest is about the cycle of reaping resources from the earth. Harvest's particular unique powers also deal with foresight and finding things, because that is the point of horticulture and husbanding resources, whether as humans or as other animals.<br /> <br /> <b>Fox, Vermillion and Wise</b>, has the Arcanum of Mind. Fox is about insight and understanding, yes, but Fox is primarily about cunning. They are a fox, and the epitome of small, cunning predators. The wisdom of Fox is pretty much a side effect of everything else about them. Fox is wise because fox is cunning, and curious; all traits necessary to the survival of small predators.<br /> <br /> Following that train of thought, Deer is, ultimately, about the <i>end </i>of the Hunt. The Horned King has his reign, he is virile and powerful and majestic for his season, brooks no challengers, defeats all enemies, evades every hunter, until the time comes and a worthy predator tracks him down. The Horned King is god-as-sacrifice, and its greatest power lies in its death, and in its seasonal return from death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 05-06-2018, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T09:46:59-07:00","id":1215833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215825#post1215825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Deer, my hypothetical &quot;Greatest Prey&quot; would have Death as their Arcana. The Influences of Pangaeans are for what they <i>are</i> while the Arcana are what they <i>mean</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Reflection, Bright and Empty</b>, has the Arcana of Prime and, to a lesser extent, Forces. Reflection is perception, and perception is Truth, hence Prime, whereas Forces impacts light. Its Influences are, quite directly, Reflections, but also Water, because water is the primary reflective surface of the Neolithic era.<br /> <br /> <b>Harvest, Watchful and Ravenous</b>, has the Arcanum of Matter. Matter is about the manipulation and categorization of resources, which is very much Harvest's jam. Their Influences are Hunger and Foraging, because Harvest is about the cycle of reaping resources from the earth. Harvest's particular unique powers also deal with foresight and finding things, because that is the point of horticulture and husbanding resources, whether as humans or as other animals.<br /> <br /> <b>Fox, Vermillion and Wise</b>, has the Arcanum of Mind. Fox is about insight and understanding, yes, but Fox is primarily about cunning. They are a fox, and the epitome of small, cunning predators. The wisdom of Fox is pretty much a side effect of everything else about them. Fox is wise because fox is cunning, and curious; all traits necessary to the survival of small predators.<br /> <br /> Following that train of thought, Deer is, ultimately, about the <i>end </i>of the Hunt. The Horned King has his reign, he is virile and powerful and majestic for his season, brooks no challengers, defeats all enemies, evades every hunter, until the time comes and a worthy predator tracks him down. The Horned King is god-as-sacrifice, and its greatest power lies in its death, and in its seasonal return from death.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are very good observations. I might take notes from this with how I work out the Pangaean version of Aharnuz and revisit my Sundered World writeup for the Deep. <br /> <br /> What about Turtle? I made his Arcana primarily Life and Death, with a bit of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T10:01:11-07:00","id":1215836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215825#post1215825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following that train of thought, Deer is, ultimately, about the <i>end </i>of the Hunt. The Horned King has his reign, he is virile and powerful and majestic for his season, brooks no challengers, defeats all enemies, evades every hunter, until the time comes and a worthy predator tracks him down. The Horned King is god-as-sacrifice, and its greatest power lies in its death, and in its seasonal return from death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what came to my mind when suggesting Life and Death for Deer. The cycle of life, death and life out of death.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T00:15:55-07:00","id":1216005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215836#post1215836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's what came to my mind when suggesting Life and Death for Deer. The cycle of life, death and life out of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, assuming he'd be Rank 8 like Wolf, would Deer have four dots each in Life and Death? Also, I gave Turtle a power based on that Optional Rule from Optional Mysteries which allowed him to cast above the limits of his Arcana, so maybe Deer could have that as well?<br /> <br /> And maybe you could reskin the Immortal Dread Power from the CofD rulebook. I know Pangaeans can come back to life if their hearts are left undisturbed, but maybe Deer stands out somehow in this aspect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-07-2018, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T00:52:06-07:00","id":1216010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216005#post1216005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, assuming he'd be Rank 8 like Wolf, would Deer have four dots each in Life and Death? Also, I gave Turtle a power based on that Optional Rule from Optional Mysteries which allowed him to cast above the limits of his Arcana, so maybe Deer could have that as well?<br /> <br /> And maybe you could reskin the Immortal Dread Power from the CofD rulebook. I know Pangaeans can come back to life if their hearts are left undisturbed, but maybe Deer stands out somehow in this aspect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was Wolf Rank 8? Anyway, somehow I feel Deer would be a Rank or two lower than Wolf, with Prey being a concept subservient to Predation. But that\u2019s just me. <br /> <br /> And I do love the traditionally Lovecraftian image of \u201cdead and dreaming\u201d being applied to the traditionally nature/pagan/Wicca image of Deer. <br /> <br /> Oh, and I feel if Deer has to have a second Arcana other than Death, it\u2019d be Spirit for better contrast with Wolf.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe one of Deer\u2019s powers (Dread Powers? Numina?) enable Him to return to life when killed in a way that is framed as a hunt, and even when not still return to life when the world sees a \u201cgreat hunter\u201d (ie. Wolf\u2019s inheritor).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-07-2018, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T05:59:35-07:00","id":1216065,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure Wolf was the biggest effin' Pangean, period. At least Rank wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T07:16:34-07:00","id":1216101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216065#post1216065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly sure Wolf was the biggest effin' Pangean, period. At least Rank wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>...did he CREATE Pangaea, though? If not, then whatever <i>that entity</i> is, would be the Big Boss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T07:19:05-07:00","id":1216102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216101#post1216101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...did he CREATE Pangaea, though? If not, then whatever <i>that entity</i> is, would be the Big Boss.</div> </div> </div> </div>His death destroyed it- so it may be close enough :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T07:20:07-07:00","id":1216104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216101#post1216101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...did he CREATE Pangaea, though? If not, then whatever <i>that entity</i> is, would be the Big Boss.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAs the Sundered World indicates, the werewolves certainly tell stories that Wolf brought Pangaea into being in order to satisfy its primal urge to patrol and hunt on its boundary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T07:24:05-07:00","id":1216108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216101#post1216101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...did he CREATE Pangaea, though? If not, then whatever <i>that entity</i> is, would be the Big Boss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crazy theory; Gaia, the hypothetical Rank 9 spirit of the Earth, isn\u2019t a spirit in the traditional sense, nor a Pangaean. Pangaea was Her physical body, the Shadow is Her spirit, and the Dark Mother of the Begotten is Her mind. When Pangaea was destroyed with the death of Wolf, its lynchpin, She shed a ghost that descended to the Underworld and drank a good deal of its waters just to make room, and is now known as the Leviathan of the Ocean of Fragments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T07:38:04-07:00","id":1216115,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> I'll have to take a better look at Turtle, and at actual lore around turtles, before I can comment.<br /> <br /> With regards to Deer, I would argue that the prey is not subservient to the predator. If anything, it's the other way around. Even the most successful pack hunters in the world, African Wild Dogs, only kill their prey sixty percent of the time. Except where their population is so enormous that they might outnumber their prey thirty to one, then it's ninety percent of the time. Predators depend on their prey for sustenance.<br /> <br /> I definitely think that Deer would be of equal Rank to Wolf, and would have some unique powers that interact with the Sacred Hunt like Reflection does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T07:49:07-07:00","id":1216119,"title":"","content":"&quot;The entire balance of the world is reworked as the Great Predator\u2019s dying howl forces a new form of harmony between flesh and spirit.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;As well as Influences and Numina, a Pangaean also possesses Arcana dots equal to its Rank. It casts spells using its Rank instead of Gnosis. <i>Many Pangaeans also possess other unique powers over the world.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> If any Pangaean has unique powers it'd be Father Wolf. If you want Pangaeans with the same Rank as Urfarah (which I personally prefer) you could make a claim that it wasn't his death that transformed the Border Marches; it was his last act that did. The shattered souls of Rat and Spider can destroy or reinforce the Gauntlet, and what's to say their Pangaean forms couldn't do even more to the Border Marches before they were shattered? If so, Wolf wouldn't be the only Pangaean with influence over the shape of the Border Marches. It's the scale of his influence that was unique.<br /> And remember that the most cited reason for why Urfarah was killed was because of him showing weakness. I seriously doubt that would happen if he was one whole Rank above everyone else instead of simply being the strongest on his Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-07-2018, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T08:29:00-07:00","id":1216146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216119#post1216119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any Pangaean has unique powers it'd be Father Wolf. If you want Pangaeans with the same Rank as Urfarah (which I personally prefer) you could make a claim that it wasn't his death that transformed the Border Marches; it was his last act that did. The shattered souls of Rat and Spider can destroy or reinforce the Gauntlet, and what's to say their Pangaean forms couldn't do even more to the Border Marches before they were shattered? If so, Wolf wouldn't be the only Pangaean with influence over the shape of the Border Marches. It's the scale of his influence that was unique.<br /> And remember that the most cited reason for why Urfarah was killed was because of him showing weakness. I seriously doubt that would happen if he was one whole Rank above everyone else instead of simply being the strongest on his Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Uratha finally realized &quot;Hey, we could take this motherfucker.&quot; And they did. Because they were built for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T08:29:16-07:00","id":1216147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216010#post1216010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, and I feel if Deer has to have a second Arcana other than Death, it\u2019d be Spirit for better contrast with Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know- deer are a strong symbol of vitality, rebirth and, well, life. There is a reason why Stag is Life's Aeon, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T08:52:53-07:00","id":1216158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216147#post1216147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know- deer are a strong symbol of vitality, rebirth and, well, life. There is a reason why Stag is Life's Aeon, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was using Arcanist\u2019s observations of Is and Means for my interpretation. Stag/Deer is a being of vitality and life, but not as its giver or master, but as a bearer of it. All so he can be the perfect prey. The cycle of the hunt is not merely vigorous but spiritual, especially in the age of Pangaea, thus my preference for Spirit. And again, better contrast with Wolf.<br /> <br /> (Honestly, I\u2019d even have only Death as Deer/Stag\u2019s Arcanum, emphasizing the contrast even further, and leave any life-related powers to Influences, Numina and those unique Pangaean powers we don\u2019t have a named category for. The charm of Pangaeans for me is that their Awakened power is only a part of their might, and I feel focusing too much on their Arcana detracts from that.)<br /> <br /> (And was Stag specifically Life\u2019s Aeon? Hmm, I\u2019ll have to reread Astral Realms some time)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T09:11:38-07:00","id":1216161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216146#post1216146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Uratha finally realized &quot;Hey, we could take this motherfucker.&quot; And they did. Because they were built for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong, but how is it relevant to my suggestion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T09:59:15-07:00","id":1216186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216161#post1216161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not wrong, but how is it relevant to my suggestion?</div> </div> </div> </div>The general notion is that Wolf kept the spirit world and the physical one separate. Logic would dictate that he had the capacity to do this (and I'm using the pronoun here extremely loosely, as loosely as a primal form of the universe has a right to them). Still, he was only one, hence why he sired his progeny, logically.<br /> <br /> And he made them capable of shredding Pangaeans. Which implies he himself, was able to do this, because of how influences work, or because he had that much more rank over any other. The distinction is irrelevant, he was a force to be beyond reckoned with. I believe we'd do him a disservice by presenting Pangaens that could conceivably match him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:21:45-07:00","id":1216192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216158#post1216158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was using Arcanist\u2019s observations of Is and Means for my interpretation. Stag/Deer is a being of vitality and life, but not as its giver or master, but as a bearer of it. All so he can be the perfect prey. The cycle of the hunt is not merely vigorous but spiritual, especially in the age of Pangaea, thus my preference for Spirit. And again, better contrast with Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must ask- where did Father Wolf's Arcana were stated? I don't remember seeing them in Sundered World, and I simply assumed they would probably be Life and Spirit, as those are the Arcana associated with the Uratha themselves.<br /> <br /> Also, as Deer would definitely have a Rank above 5 (if Wolf is 8, I assume 7), it has to have another Arcana other than Death, by RAW, even if it is one to two dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 05-07-2018, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:25:03-07:00","id":1216194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216186#post1216186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general notion is that Wolf kept the spirit world and the physical one separate. Logic would dictate that he had the capacity to do this (and I'm using the pronoun here extremely loosely, as loosely as a primal form of the universe has a right to them). Still, he was only one, hence why he sired his progeny, logically.<br /> <br /> And he made them capable of shredding Pangaeans. Which implies he himself, was able to do this, because of how influences work, or because he had that much more rank over any other. The distinction is irrelevant, he was a force to be beyond reckoned with. I believe we'd do him a disservice by presenting Pangaens that could conceivably match him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad interpretation, but my suggestion was not &quot;this is how it probably was&quot; but rather &quot;this is how you could rationalise Wolf sharing Rank with other Pangaeans, if that's what you want for your setting&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with both possibilities. I just personally think one is more interesting than the other. In my opinion allowing other Pangaeans to share Rank with Wolf doesn't diminish his impact in the setting (creation of Uratha and the Firstborn, imposing a law over all other Pangaeans, and transforming the Border Marches into the Gauntlet) but rather allows other Pangaeans to also achieve feats of the same magnitude. <i>That</i> I find much more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:33:13-07:00","id":1216199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216194#post1216194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not a bad interpretation, but my suggestion was not &quot;this is how it probably was&quot; but rather &quot;this is how you could rationalise Wolf sharing Rank with other Pangaeans, if that's what you want for your setting&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with both possibilities. I just personally think one is more interesting than the other. In my opinion allowing other Pangaeans to share Rank with Wolf doesn't diminish his impact in the setting (creation of Uratha and the Firstborn, imposing a law over all other Pangaeans, and transforming the Border Marches into the Gauntlet) but rather allows other Pangaeans to also achieve feats of the same magnitude. <i>That</i> I find much more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather start with what those feats are than make the Pangean first, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:35:00-07:00","id":1216200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1215310#post1215310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019d say one for a generic type of animal. One Turtle, one Cat, one Hyena, so on and so forth. Pangaeans are epic entities that had a Realm all their own. I\u2019d keep their population low, to help preserve their aura of savage grandeur.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perspective understood... however that raises a few questions:<br /> <br /> 1. How many Pangaeans are really around for the Wise to poach and steal their hearts to use? The known list only includes a few examples of their victims. The text mentions that &quot;...a dozen lesser gods of the Border Marches now lie as festering carcasses.&quot; If the Wise of the Vinca are the same elsewhere, then surely Wolf's howl was as much to protect the Border Marches from humans flipping the script on Pangaeans as it was to protect the material world from spiritual intrusion!<br /> <br /> 2. How many Pangaeans are around for their grand, predator-prey relationships to play out in? Noted is the observation that if the heart is left undisturbed a Pangaean will reform, however we have a raft of examples of Wolf's victims that he killed so hard they ended up as Shartha! Plus, the Pangaean Firstborn apparently ate Wolf's heart when they killed him, or we'd have him back by now (barring some strange interaction with the collapse of Pangaea into the Gauntlet).<br /> <br /> 3. The existence of the Firstborn themselves stands as an indication that greater Pangeans could spawn lesser. Wolf could not have been the only one to try this, surely?<br /> <br /> 4. Sundered World notes that &quot;...shattered fragments of old gods all threaten [humanity's civilization].&quot; While that could be read in context as referring to the Time Before, it could also be assumed to refer to the side-effect of the Pangaean predation cycle.<br /> <br /> Since as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> helpfully points out, we don't actually have published, canon (versus &quot;official&quot; Chris Allen) stats for Pangaeans, then the question of who is out there becomes a matter for your table and story, as well as the fun of an academic exercise. Sundered World just mentioned ones we could consider &quot;high&quot; level Pangaeans, with we what we can assume is significant influence to the Vinca (and among the natural cycles of the world--though it mentions they are mutable creatures): The Bull, the Bird, the Snake, the Cat, the Fox, the Wolf, the Boar and The River. Wolf is mentioned as being central to the pantheon [of the Vinca], however we could surmise if needed that a different People might have structured their own pantheon a little differently based on the influencing gods at work. To reinforce this point, each of the (non-canon) write-ups of a Pangaean limits the geographic reach of their powers. Surely they did wander, however you wouldn't get a response from Bull regarding your cattle if he's always a few thousand miles away meddling in India. (Admittedly this example is flawed, as Bull handed out bits of his heart as stones, and could presumably use those as receiving stations for petitions....)<br /> <br /> In any event, I really appreciate the comments on structure and theme for Pangaeans reflected (ha) in this thread. <br /> <br /> Another thought: certainly Wolf's death-howl had world-wide consequences, and certainly within his purview he was a foremost predator in Pangaea, but what if there were others who filled his shoes in other parts of the world when he was off ranging across his preferred grounds? <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T14:44:57-07:00","id":1216311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216192#post1216192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must ask- where did Father Wolf's Arcana were stated? I remember seeing them in Sundered World, and I simply assumed they would probably be Life and Spirit, as those are the Arcana associated with the Uratha themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Huh, now that you point it out, I can\u2019t recall a published source. I remember a mention that Wolf would have all His Arcana dots in Spirit, but I can\u2019t recall from where... ignore me on this one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, as Deer would definitely have a Rank above 5 (if Wolf is 8, I assume 7), it has to have another Arcana other than Death, by RAW, even if it is one to two dots. </div> </div> </div>Aww, no room for Archmastery? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T14:55:27-07:00","id":1216322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216200#post1216200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. How many Pangaeans are around for their grand, predator-prey relationships to play out in? Noted is the observation that if the heart is left undisturbed a Pangaean will reform, however we have a raft of examples of Wolf's victims that he killed so hard they ended up as Shartha! Plus, the Pangaean Firstborn apparently ate Wolf's heart when they killed him, or we'd have him back by now (barring some strange interaction with the collapse of Pangaea into the Gauntlet).</div> </div> </div> </div>We're not quite sure what causes shartha, but one of the theories for their existence is that Father Wolf didn't manage to kill them, which is why they broke apart on their own into the hosts. Presumably this is what leads to some people thinking werewolves are hosts, with them effectively being or containing pieces of Father Wolf's heart. In this case it's likely not the Firstborn that ate his heart, but the Uratha.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thought: certainly Wolf's death-howl had world-wide consequences, and certainly within his purview he was a foremost predator in Pangaea, but what if there were others who filled his shoes in other parts of the world when he was off ranging across his preferred grounds? </div> </div> </div>That seems to be what the Uratha are all about. While Father Wolf is legended to have the entirety of Pangaea as his territory, the Uratha are more assuredly a global thing, appearing wherever humans are even well before the days of the Vinca settlements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-07-2018, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T15:43:19-07:00","id":1216346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216192#post1216192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must ask- where did Father Wolf's Arcana were stated? I don't remember seeing them in Sundered World, and I simply assumed they would probably be Life and Spirit, as those are the Arcana associated with the Uratha themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall if he had any Arcana stated anywhere, but my personal theory is Spirit primary and Space secondary. He is the hunt, and the hunt is all about where you are relative to your prey, closing distance, finding hiding places. It also fits into my personal theory of why Pangaea collapsed without shortly after his death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 05-07-2018, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T16:09:28-07:00","id":1216363,"title":"","content":"Perhaps off-topic considering the thread title, but - as a thought experiment - what would a Rank 1 Pangaean look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T16:21:53-07:00","id":1216368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216363#post1216363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps off-topic considering the thread title, but - as a thought experiment - what would a Rank 1 Pangaean look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like Cryptids from Summoners (Mage 1E), I assume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T17:09:14-07:00","id":1216387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1049973#post1049973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Owl behind the strix?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say no. Strix are from the Lower Depths. Now, an owl Pangaean might <i>associate</i> with Strix...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T17:11:08-07:00","id":1216388,"title":"","content":"<i>Urfarah</i> might\u2019ve had Space and Spirit, considering his obsessive need to patrol the Border Marches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T17:42:30-07:00","id":1216398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216368#post1216368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something like Cryptids from Summoners (Mage 1E), I assume.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant as a being, lore-wise, as opposed to mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T17:49:29-07:00","id":1216400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216398#post1216398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant as a being, lore-wise, as opposed to mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beings of half Life and half Spirit who live in places where the Flesh and the Shadow cross. Sounds a lot like Pangaeans, but degraded and degenerated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T18:04:00-07:00","id":1216403,"title":"","content":"In regards to beings the same Rank as Father Wolf, the Spinner Hag, Plague King, Corpse Eater, Carrion Prince, and Sea Serpent are supposed to be vast and up there. One of the (many) theories in the books suggests that there was a sort of group of demonic entities that the Spinner Hag was part of, which may have been the other host-bearing Pangaeans, the idea being that they'd split themselves up and outlast Father Wolf and the Uratha, so their shartha descendants would reform when there was no wolves to destroy them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216387#post1216387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say no. Strix are from the Lower Depths. Now, an owl Pangaean might <i>associate</i> with Strix...</div> </div> </div> </div>When Pangaea fell, most became spirits, but some became other things. It's always possible one became the strix, or the lower depth they're supposed to be from is a Pangaean hidey-hole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216363#post1216363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps off-topic considering the thread title, but - as a thought experiment - what would a Rank 1 Pangaean look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something insignificant? It's probably why there's no such thing.'Pangaeans are always at least Rank 3, and usually Rank 5 or more.' Insignificance and weakness don't seem to have a place in Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-07-2018, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T22:47:00-07:00","id":1216501,"title":"","content":"-nevermind-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T06:23:19-07:00","id":1216603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216322#post1216322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're not quite sure what causes shartha, but one of the theories for their existence is that Father Wolf didn't manage to kill them, which is why they broke apart on their own into the hosts. Presumably this is what leads to some people thinking werewolves are hosts, with them effectively being or containing pieces of Father Wolf's heart. In this case it's likely not the Firstborn that ate his heart, but the Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>So. We could surmise that Father Wolf didn't actually <i>kill</i>-kill other Pangaeans, by consuming their hearts and destroying their ability to reform--he just chased them around and ate the non-essential parts when he caught them because that's what predators do. Oh. And in doing so (selecting targets) he chased off spirits that transgressed into the material world? I may be confusing the role assumed by the Uratha afterward, with Wolf.... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216322#post1216322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems to be what the Uratha are all about. While Father Wolf is legended to have the entirety of Pangaea as his territory, the Uratha are more assuredly a global thing, appearing wherever humans are even well before the days of the Vinca settlements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure: the cosmology of the Uratha is pretty tight and you can stop there with some satisfaction. Wolf hunts, and begets the Firstborn who hunt with him and with each other, and they beget the Secondborn and the Uratha and everyone hunts everywhere and the spirits are annoyed because they rain on the essence parade that should be occurring. No other predatory animals are necessary (except maybe sea-dwelling ones) and it's OK to ignore ursines, felines and raptors because even though they are apex creatures in their domains we're talking supernatural spirit-flesh hybrids, so all other creatures can be assigned spirit analogs but not shapeshifting blends/invested Pangaeans.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are sufficient for the cosmology. Full stop. (They're also necessary, because Father Wolf folded up the Border Marches as his last [Space!/Spirit!] act, and that's important.)<br /> <br /> The only reason to have other Pangaeans, aside from &quot;Father Wolf the uber-spirit of the hunt&quot; is to a) give him a challenge in a setting (Sundered World) in which he's alive, and b) give the Wise something to poach as a sterling example of mage hubris at work.<br /> <br /> Since Wolf occupies all of the cosmological space for predators, if we care to theorize his peers of the time we can either suggest conceptual Pangaeans or prey entities. Or, Wolf can shoulder aside a tad and coexist with someone else who eats creatures--as occurs in our material ecologies. Personally it seems more interesting for him to share the space, even as we acknowledge his importance to the Border Marches.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T07:36:43-07:00","id":1216637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216603#post1216603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So. We could surmise that Father Wolf didn't actually <i>kill</i>-kill other Pangaeans, by consuming their hearts and destroying their ability to reform--he just chased them around and ate the non-essential parts when he caught them because that's what predators do. Oh. And in doing so (selecting targets) he chased off spirits that transgressed into the material world? I may be confusing the role assumed by the Uratha afterward, with Wolf....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But if that's the case- than why did the pangaeans self destroyed their own hearts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T08:15:45-07:00","id":1216663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216637#post1216637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if that's the case- than why did the pangaeans self destroyed their own hearts?</div> </div> </div> </div>But only in the case of Bull and Bird (for the Vinca, that is), and because the People represented their interests in civilization. They wished for the Wise to shepherd the People well, and gave them the means to easily contact them. &quot;Each of the original omphalos stones is a fragment of the Bull or the Bird\u2019s heart. Most stand twice the height of a man...&quot;<br /> <br /> The indication is that the full hearts are both larger in size and, by inference with the Watchtower analogs, may grow over time--or shrink.<br /> <br /> Regardless, it seems as though gifting a chuck of heart didn't slow Bull and Bird down too much... though IIRC eventually the greedy Wise hunted them down and took what was left.<br /> <br /> In some respects this whole heart-business reflects the story of the golden goose, only in this case the goose gets ripped open and a prize found, albeit once. If the Wise had been clever enough to meet their Pangaean counterparts with something that interested them, they could have negotiated the pieces they needed--but they were too impatient to do so, and in response drove a wedge between humanity and their gods.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T08:35:15-07:00","id":1216672,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed the tidbit describing Pangaeans as \u2018animal-headed\u2019\u2014-indicating they can, at whim, become very much like the depictions of Egyptian deities.<br /> <br /> ...speaking of which, since the Border Marches covered the entire planet, what would the Pangaeans of the area that would eventually become Irem, and, later on Egypt, have been up to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T08:45:25-07:00","id":1216679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216603#post1216603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. We could surmise that Father Wolf didn't actually <i>kill</i>-kill other Pangaeans, by consuming their hearts and destroying their ability to reform--he just chased them around and ate the non-essential parts when he caught them because that's what predators do. Oh. And in doing so (selecting targets) he chased off spirits that transgressed into the material world? I may be confusing the role assumed by the Uratha afterward, with Wolf....</div> </div> </div> </div>He could have been a predator that let worthy prey resurrect. I was more suggesting that these other Pangaeans were called out by name books ago and were really powerful (or just made a nuisance of themselves when Father Wolf weakened).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure: the cosmology of the Uratha is pretty tight and you can stop there with some satisfaction. Wolf hunts, and begets the Firstborn who hunt with him and with each other, and they beget the Secondborn and the Uratha and everyone hunts everywhere and the spirits are annoyed because they rain on the essence parade that should be occurring. No other predatory animals are necessary (except maybe sea-dwelling ones) and it's OK to ignore ursines, felines and raptors because even though they are apex creatures in their domains we're talking supernatural spirit-flesh hybrids, so all other creatures can be assigned spirit analogs but not shapeshifting blends/invested Pangaeans. </div> </div> </div>The Firstborn didn't beget the Uratha. They've been tied with Father Wolf and Luna since the very beginning. The Firstborn would later become tribal totems..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolves are sufficient for the cosmology. Full stop. (They're also necessary, because Father Wolf folded up the Border Marches as his last [Space!/Spirit!] act, and that's important.) </div> </div> </div>We do have some other were-creatures (the Baal-Hadad, for instance). I just wouldn't go so far as to say every Pangaean has Pangaean-people. It's a possibility, but a very slim one. And mostly irrelevant, as if they did there's no evidence of them even in Pangaean times, as they're long extinct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only reason to have other Pangaeans, aside from &quot;Father Wolf the uber-spirit of the hunt&quot; is to a) give him a challenge in a setting (Sundered World) in which he's alive, and b) give the Wise something to poach as a sterling example of mage hubris at work. </div> </div> </div>It allows for the creation of hosts in the modern age, though those can also be linked to idigam.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since Wolf occupies all of the cosmological space for predators, if we care to theorize his peers of the time we can either suggest conceptual Pangaeans or prey entities. Or, Wolf can shoulder aside a tad and coexist with someone else who eats creatures--as occurs in our material ecologies. Personally it seems more interesting for him to share the space, even as we acknowledge his importance to the Border Marches. </div> </div> </div>That's why I suggested Spinner Hag (Spider), Plague King (Rat), Carrion Prince and Corpse Eater (Crows) and the others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216672#post1216672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really enjoyed the tidbit describing Pangaeans as \u2018animal-headed\u2019\u2014-indicating they can, at whim, become very much like the depictions of Egyptian deities.<br /> <br /> ...speaking of which, since the Border Marches covered the entire planet, what would the Pangaeans of the area that would eventually become Irem, and, later on Egypt, have been up to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that section was actually referring to the Gods of Irem, who may not have been Pangaeans. It's in a sidebar dedicated to talking about other gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T08:53:27-07:00","id":1216684,"title":"","content":"Would the Shan\u2019iatu have been the Lower Depths equivalent of Pangaeans, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T08:59:02-07:00","id":1216687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216663#post1216663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But only in the case of Bull and Bird (for the Vinca, that is), and because the People represented their interests in civilization. They wished for the Wise to shepherd the People well, and gave them the means to easily contact them. &quot;Each of the original omphalos stones is a fragment of the Bull or the Bird\u2019s heart. Most stand twice the height of a man...&quot;<br /> <br /> The indication is that the full hearts are both larger in size and, by inference with the Watchtower analogs, may grow over time--or shrink.<br /> <br /> Regardless, it seems as though gifting a chuck of heart didn't slow Bull and Bird down too much... though IIRC eventually the greedy Wise hunted them down and took what was left.<br /> <br /> In some respects this whole heart-business reflects the story of the golden goose, only in this case the goose gets ripped open and a prize found, albeit once. If the Wise had been clever enough to meet their Pangaean counterparts with something that interested them, they could have negotiated the pieces they needed--but they were too impatient to do so, and in response drove a wedge between humanity and their gods.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I talked about how Spider and Rat turned into hosts to avoid death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T09:01:12-07:00","id":1216688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216687#post1216687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I talked about how Spider and Rat turned into hosts to avoid death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either it's a lie, or they did some mystical mumbo-jumbo that split their soul-stones into smaller pieces, or imbued them into servant creatures. This might be why Ariadne has generated an omphalos stone inside her, from collecting tiny pieces in the form of soul shards from so many other azlu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216684#post1216684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the Shan\u2019iatu have been the Lower Depths equivalent of Pangaeans, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if that would be a useful comparison, Lower Depths are a wide range of things. It's possible Azar was a Pangaean, but I expect that would put the Mummy fandom in an uproar. I'm just guessing but I figure they see Azar and the Shan'iatu as 'its own thing.' Which is entirely fair, there's a <i>lot</i> of stuff in the Chronicles of Darkness and most of it doesn't seem related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-08-2018, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T09:08:23-07:00","id":1216694,"title":"","content":"I always just saw Azar as a VERY powerful Shan\u2019iatu, myself. He was MUCH wiser than his siblings, and so he got tasked with tutoring the other Shan\u2019iatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T09:18:17-07:00","id":1216698,"title":"","content":"And to clarify, I myself do not hold to the idea Shan\u2019iatu were Pangaeans. I was merely floating forward an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T09:59:18-07:00","id":1216715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216687#post1216687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I talked about how Spider and Rat turned into hosts to avoid death.</div> </div> </div> </div>At another point in the DE, Father Wolf is described as &quot;shattering the souls&quot; in his jaws of some Pangaens who transgressed. That implies shattering their heart-stones, which implies little shards, which could immediately lead to Shartha. After all if Wolf gets to wipe out the Border Marches as his death-act, then why can't lesser prey break themselves? Rhetorical question--the answer is the Azlu and Beshilu, among others.<br /> <br /> Correction received: Firstborn not linked to Uratha. Wolf+wolfspirit = Firstborn. Wolf+Luna (maybe) = Uratha. Or not. Depending on desired legend.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> I'm glad we agree that there's space for other Pangaeans of predatory sorts. I'd also be alarmed if every Pangaean had their were-creature counterpart, if simply because that's an unnecessarily reductive explanation for a rare shapeshifter in your story. How many people need detailed backstories and lore to explain the weird guy who turns into an orca? (For example. Orcas are cool, y0.)<br /> <br /> The Darkness is a very accepting and tolerant place.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T10:29:51-07:00","id":1216728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216715#post1216715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At another point in the DE, Father Wolf is described as &quot;shattering the souls&quot; in his jaws of some Pangaens who transgressed. That implies shattering their heart-stones, which implies little shards, which could immediately lead to Shartha. After all if Wolf gets to wipe out the Border Marches as his death-act, then why can't lesser prey break themselves? Rhetorical question--the answer is the Azlu and Beshilu, among others.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, but if Wolf never planned on destroying those pangaeans, only kill them and allow them to reform, why would they destroy themselves? The quote itself suggest that Father Wolf did planned on destroying Spider, Rat and the rest, and their shattering is either the result, or a means for them to escape an even more permanent death (for example, perhaps as a God of the Hunt, one of his unique powers actually allow him to destroy any pangaean he shatters, or something like that). <br /> <br /> As for secondary predator pangaeans, I suggest Jaguar- in Skinchangers he is detailed as a parallel to Father Wolf, close to him even if not equal. Besides, the Balam Colop had to come from somewhere. In my head canon he, like Bull, has turned Infernal- even though the process, reasons and result are quit different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T10:58:45-07:00","id":1216738,"title":"","content":"I'd be sorely disappointed if Shark was not a badass Pangean predator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T11:02:05-07:00","id":1216742,"title":"","content":"Or Whale being flat-out huge beyond belief, absurd in its sheer bulk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T13:05:18-07:00","id":1216781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216742#post1216742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Whale being flat-out huge beyond belief, absurd in its sheer bulk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whale: Leviathan and Majestic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T13:07:46-07:00","id":1216783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216781#post1216781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whale: Leviathan and Majestic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Powerful and Majestic perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T13:12:06-07:00","id":1216785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216728#post1216728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, but if Wolf never planned on destroying those pangaeans, only kill them and allow them to reform, why would they destroy themselves? The quote itself suggest that Father Wolf did planned on destroying Spider, Rat and the rest, and their shattering is either the result, or a means for them to escape an even more permanent death (for example, perhaps as a God of the Hunt, one of his unique powers actually allow him to destroy any pangaean he shatters, or something like that).<br /> <br /> As for secondary predator pangaeans, I suggest Jaguar- in Skinchangers he is detailed as a parallel to Father Wolf, close to him even if not equal. Besides, the Balam Colop had to come from somewhere. In my head canon he, like Bull, has turned Infernal- even though the process, reasons and result are quit different.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The main Shartha seem to be Rat and Spider--both of whom managed to honk off Father Wolf enough that we can assume he intended to end them. Certainly Urfarah <i>could </i>have killed any other Pangaean he was able to physically subdue; if not, then he's a poor apex predator. At the same time, other Pangaeans are only speed bumps if it's that &quot;simple&quot; to get rid of them, primal pillars of concepts and natural order that they are! As in most things, there's probably a balance in perspective to hit, here.<br /> <br /> The Wise and their heart-stealing ways are presented as an aberration that bore the potential to up-end order. That was one reason for even the patron gods of the People to turn away from them (the Wise).<br /> <br /> And yeah, Jaguar is on my mental list. Then there should be others, who are remembered as iconic figures of hunting, predation and natural war across cultures. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T13:27:10-07:00","id":1216791,"title":"","content":"Whale would have some dominion over singing, for rather obvious reasons. For Arcana, I\u2019d say Mind and Space: Mind because of the complexity and beauty of whalesong; and Space because he casts his song to all corners of the ocean (helped out by his Influences).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T13:37:24-07:00","id":1216793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216791#post1216791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whale would have some dominion over singing, for rather obvious reasons. For Arcana, I\u2019d say Mind and Space: Mind because of the complexity and beauty of whalesong; and Space because he casts his song to all corners of the ocean (helped out by his Influences).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see both Arcana working for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T13:52:57-07:00","id":1216802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1045886-the-lords-of-pangaea-today?p=1216791#post1216791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whale would have some dominion over singing, for rather obvious reasons. For Arcana, I\u2019d say Mind and Space: Mind because of the complexity and beauty of whalesong; and Space because he casts his song to all corners of the ocean (helped out by his Influences).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh much better!<br /> <br /> <i>Whale: Leviathan and Melodious</i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.the